248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (An SQL database works by organizing data into tables, each containing rows and columns. It uses a structured query language \(SQL\) to interact with the data. Users can perform operations like inserting, updating, deleting, and querying data using SQL commands. The database engine manages tasks like storing and retrieving data efficiently, ensuring data integrity through constraints, and optimizing queries for performance.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
