263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (In SQL, there are mainly three types of commands:)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 878 0 R
/ActualText (Data Manipulation Language \(DML\) commands: These commands are used to manipulate data stored in the database. Common DML commands include SELECT \(retrieve data\), INSERT \(insert new data\), UPDATE \(modify existing data\), and DELETE \(remove data\).)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 879 0 R
/ActualText (Data Definition Language \(DDL\) commands: These commands are used to define and manage the structure of the database objects. Common DDL commands include CREATE \(create new objects like tables, indexes, etc.\), ALTER \(modify existing objects\), and DROP \(delete objects\).)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 880 0 R
/ActualText (Data Control Language \(DCL\) commands: These commands are used to control access to data within the database. Common DCL commands include GRANT \(give privileges to users\), REVOKE \(take away privileges from users\), etc.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
