/T (30. What are the benefits of SQL database over NoSQL database?)
/E (30. What are the benefits of SQL database over NoSQL database?)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( SQL databases offer structured data storage, ensuring data consistency and integrity through predefined schemas. They excel in complex queries and transactions, making them ideal for applications requiring ACID properties. NoSQL databases, on the other hand, are flexible, scalable, and suitable for unstructured or semi-structured data. They handle large volumes of data and are adept at distributed computing. Choosing between them depends on the specific needs of the project, with SQL databases favored for transactional systems and NoSQL databases for handling big data and scalability.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
