/T (31. What is a constraint, and why use constraints?)
/E (31. What is a constraint, and why use constraints?)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A constraint is a limitation or restriction placed on a system or process. We use constraints to guide and control various aspects of a project or process, ensuring it stays within predefined boundaries and achieves specific goals effectively. Constraints help in managing resources efficiently, improving focus, and delivering results within set parameters.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
