/S /H2
/T (32. What is a SQL operator?)
/E (32. What is a SQL operator?)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
431 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A SQL operator is a symbol or keyword used to perform operations on data in a database, such as comparison, arithmetic, or logical operations. Examples include "=", "<>", "AND", "OR", "+", "-", "*", and "/".)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
