/Pg 20 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A table is a database object that stores data in rows and columns, like a spreadsheet. A view, on the other hand, is a virtual table generated by a query. It doesn't store data itself but presents data from one or more tables based on the query criteria.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (44. Describe the process of database sharding.)
/E (44. Describe the process of database sharding.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
486 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Database sharding is the process of horizontally partitioning data across multiple servers. Each partition, or shard, contains a subset of the data. This helps distribute the load and improve scalability of the database system.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
