/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The DISTINCT statement in SQL is used to remove duplicate records from a result set. You simply include the keyword DISTINCT immediately after the SELECT keyword in your SQL query to ensure that only unique rows are returned.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
