/S /H2
/T (55. Define a temp table?)
/E (55. Define a temp table?)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText ( A temporary table is a database table that exists temporarily and is typically used for storing intermediate or temporary data within a database session. It is often used to simplify complex queries or to store results temporarily during data processing. Temporary tables are automatically dropped when the database session ends or when they are explicitly dropped by the user.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (56. What Is primary key?)
/E (56. What Is primary key?)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A primary key is a unique identifier for each record in a database table, ensuring that no two records have the same value for the primary key column. It's essential for data integrity and efficient retrieval of information.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [8]
>>
