/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (A foreign key is a column or a set of columns in a database table that establishes a link or relationship with a primary key in another table. It ensures referential integrity and helps maintain consistency and relationships between tables in a relational database.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
