600 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 923 0 R
/ActualText (Clustered indexes dictate the physical order of data in a table, while non-clustered indexes create a separate structure that points back to the original data. In simple terms, clustered indexes sort and store the data rows in the table based on their key values, while non-clustered indexes create a separate structure that holds pointers to the data rows in the table. )
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [9]
>>
